  "interpretation": "Mode C, where connectivity is perfect, is the condition that isolates snapping: per-component accuracy there rises 0.8675 -> 0.9972 and the attributed snapping headroom collapses 0.1325 -> 0.0028, so duplicate-node collapse WAS essentially the whole of it. Mean per-component accuracy in modes A and B falls slightly (-0.0040 / -0.0088), and that fall is entirely inside images whose terminal-pair F1 is below 0.5. On those, the pipeline has welded most of the drawing into one node, which makes every GT terminal-pair vacuously present and per-component accuracy read 1.0 at a terminal-pair F1 of 0.25; spreading pins across distinct nodes breaks that vacuous containment. No image at terminal-pair F1 >= 0.9 changed at all, and the count of images at F1 == 1.0 is 80 before and after, so strict success cannot move down. Mid-range images (0.5-0.9) net IMPROVED by +0.43. This is also independent evidence for the over-merge-sensitive per-component metric that is still outstanding: a metric that scores 1.0 on a prediction welding the whole page into one net is not measuring what it claims to.",
